---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// DRAFT — owner approves before publish (A8 owner prerequisites).
//
// The load-bearing honesty here (ROSETTA_FUN §8): Apple owns refunds for
// in-app purchases. We cannot process them, and this page must say so and link
// to Apple's flow rather than implying we can help.
const updated = 'July 2026';
const contact = 'support@rosetta.fun';
---

<Base title="Refunds · Rosetta" description="How refunds work, and who to ask.">
  <h1>Refunds</h1>
  <p class="faint">Last updated: {updated}</p>

  <p>
    Where you bought decides who can refund you. There are two answers, and only one of them is us.
  </p>

  <h2>Bought on this website (Stripe)</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a> within <strong>14 days</strong> and we'll refund you, as
    long as you haven't used most of what you bought. If something went wrong on our end — you were charged
    twice, or a purchase never arrived in your account — tell us whenever you notice and we'll fix it, no time
    limit.
  </p>
  <p>
    Refunds go back to the card you paid with, usually within 5–10 business days once we've issued them.
    Refunding a pack removes the credits it granted; if you've already spent them, your balance can go to
    zero but never below.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can cancel a subscription any time from <a href="/account">your account page</a>. Cancelling stops the
    next renewal — you keep what you've paid for until the period ends.
  </p>

  <h2>Bought in the iOS app (Apple)</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Apple handles those refunds, not us.</strong> We can see that a purchase happened, but we can't
    reverse the charge — Apple took the payment, and only Apple can return it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Request one at <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" rel="noopener">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>, or
    from Settings on your device. Apple decides these case by case.
  </p>
  <p>
    Manage or cancel an app subscription in <em>Settings → your name → Subscriptions</em> on your iPhone.
  </p>

  <h2>If you delete your account</h2>
  <p>
    Deleting your account is permanent and doesn't trigger a refund — remaining credits and paid time are lost.
    If you want a refund, ask for it before you delete.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p><a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a></p>
</Base>
